bibit-agenthub-plugin (0.3.11) resolute-porting; urgency=medium

  * Add a manual-refresh entry to the Agent Hub page header: an icon-only
    button (the `↻` glyph, named `Refresh` / `刷新`) sitting to the left of the
    "Create a resource" entry in the same row. It re-reads the catalog for the
    current tab and repeats the current query — same scope, agent, type, tags
    and page — so the user can pull in changes without leaving the page.
  * The entry never appears on the Settings tab. That tab reads its own
    `settings.get.v1` document and renders no catalog, so a button that
    re-reads a list it does not show would only be dead weight. The refresh
    entry stays out of the settings surface entirely.
  * Keep the in-flight read safe: while a `powers.list.v1` request is running
    the button is disabled instead of aborting and re-issuing it. Bumping the
    retry counter aborts whatever is in flight, which is the same spurious
    cancellation the window-focus refresh already avoids on the market scope.
  * The store protocol, the operation set and the Provider are untouched: the
    button reuses the page's existing retry path, so no new DTO or operation is
    introduced.

