bibit-agenthub-plugin (0.3.2) resolute-porting; urgency=medium

  * Fix a spurious "Power catalog request was cancelled" error in the Power
    market. Cancellation means "superseded" or "provider session torn down",
    not a user action, so it is now retryable and can no longer dead-end the
    page without a way out.
  * A market read that started before a newer one committed now answers from
    that newer catalog instead of reporting the supersede as a cancellation.
  * Regaining window focus no longer aborts and re-issues an in-flight read;
    it only refreshes once the view is idle.

